// NOTE: Everything here in the comments is stuff I wrote while ideating for the story. I suggest you read the story FIRST, and get unbiased views, then come back, and read this, and read it a second time, and see how well I represented all of this in the story.


// Main Theme Idea Freedom/Safety 

// Char 1 wants Freedom, Char 2 wants Safety, Char 3 wants compromise


// At story start, in a country tetering on fascism and terror. The Government whom

// Both Noelle and Dima are working on their shows, which does not seem to be stopping this, sometimes

// even supporting. Grassroots rebellions are popping up with more frequency. When they do, 

// they are shut down with little casualty, but the world is nearing a boiling point, as 

// more riots occur, and the rioters are all insulted and demeaned, causing more rioters


// Char 1 (Nico) Nikolav Sylvia (Freedom Advocate), Son, wants to overthrow current regime out of moral oblication, seen lots of suffering wants it to stop, rather strong, but may be biting off more than can be chewed in this sence, somewhat foolhearty, somewhat gullible, somewhat innocent, Currently very swayed by propaganda, may see the world as worse than it truly is.

    // ideas from the character wheel Core: Brave/Rebellious | Opposite: Cautious/Diplomatic | Adjacent Traits: Reckless, Bold | Adjacent Opposite Traits: Scared/Hesitant/Guarded

// Char 2 Noelle Sylvia (Compromise advocate), Mother, Most important thing in her life is Nikolav, Has seen lots of suffering and wants it to stop, Survived several wars already, Faith in her son, but still sees him as a baby, Ideally wants both characters to stop fighting. In particular, she saw the overthrow of a duke in her youth. She saw lots of death and despair during it, but good came later.

    // ideas from the character wheel CoreProtectiveve/Diplomatic | Opposite: Harmful/Stubborn  | Adjacent Traits: Empathetic, Mediator | Adjacent Opposite Traits: Soft/Biased

// Char 3 (Dmitri) Dmitri Sylvia (Safety advocate), Father, cares much about both other characters, no particular favorite. Has seen many rebellions and riots in his time. He believes the safest and most moral route is non-violent protests, but hypocritically will not let any of his family participate out of care for their well-being. Doesn't agree with the actions of the government he works for, but believes change is best from the inside. Took this job for good money to support his family to be intellectuals and lead the next generation of people, but through cooperation, not rebellion.

    // ideas from the character wheel Core: Protective/Calculated/Rigid | Opposite: Harmful/Foolhardy  | Adjacent Traits: Methodical/Biased/Dogmatic | Adjacent Opposite Traits: Reckless/Unempathetic
VAR ruined = false
VAR nicer = false


-> start

== start
    
The Scene opens in a large city. One would expect a city like this to be bustling, but it is rather quiet. The streets and roads are not empty, as citizens still must go about thier daily life to work to live, but many do not interact with eachother, not even looking at eachother. They hurry around quietly and in solitude. There are a few citizens on the street who act contrary to this generally accepted behavior. One greets passerby kindly, seeking acknowledgment of a petition. Many people just walk by her, and those who stop to listen typically mention they are in a hurry or late to a meeting and walk off. Another youth stands outside a large building, shouting to make their voice heard, sticking out an arm with pamphlets to passersby. Once again, they are typically ignored. Though a few pedestrians grab the flyers to read as they walk. Many watch on from nearby stores or buildings, with a somewhat cynical interest, wondering if anything will happen to this pamphlet handler. A student stands proudly at a park square, leading a march of hundreds of peers. With a marching beat and a chart on thier lips, their thoughts fill the air. Some citizens are emboldened by thier speech, seeing it as an expression of thier innermost desires they wish they could express, others see it as a pollutant. Armed guards stand near the park, ready for action if the need arises. Lastly, a figure in all black, face and hands covered, is seen in the park as well, rope in hand, approaching a statue nearby this protest. The police notice and use this as a reason to take action. Loud shouting ensues.
The Scene then shifts to one tall building in the city, far from the park, but close enough to feel its rippling. A Family sits at the dinner table. It is lit up by lights, yet still dark, and it is colder than expected after sitting out for a few hours. The night sky stars would glimmer, but they are covered by clouds. There is a silence in the air, an animosity between the youngest at the table, Nikolav, and the oldest, Dimitri. Neither dares to speak, just letting the silence build. Eventually, the mother, Noelle, cannot stand the silence anymore and stands up to get a remote to turn on the TV for background noise. A jarring sound of static, then a voice.
Newscaster: This just in, another incident of agitators at Checkfield Park was once again disrupting the peace via -
Noelle quickly changes the channel to something else.

* [Nikolav: Speak up against what's happening on the news.]-> speakup
* [Nikolav: Tell Mom we don’t need the TV.] -> antitv
* Nikolav: *Say Nothing* -> silence


== speakup

Nikolav glances at the TV and his mother fiddling with the remote, then turns his gaze towards the old man at the table as his gaze becomes a glare.
Nikolav: *Glaring at Dimitri* Does it bother you how protestors are represented on the News?
Noelle: Nico, dear, let's not talk about this right now.
Dimitri: It's fine, dear. It's an important topic.
Nikolav’s expression softens slightly, but he is still tense, suspicious.
Dimitri: Even if they are the wrong ones.
Nikolav’s brow deepens, suspicions confirmed.
Noelle: Now I wouldn’t say just that, just because they are wrong to you -

* [Nikolav Reasks his question] -> botheryou 
* [Nikolav: If I can have <i>wrong</i> opinions, then I want to go to a protest!] -> protest
* [Nikolav doesn't interrupt] -> mamatime

== mamatime

Noelle: I know how you both feel about the news, as we have talked about it a thousand times before, and I know what would make you feel heard.
Noelle: *Looking at Nikolav* You feel the world is in a dangerous state, and people have to speak up or be crushed by the current government, yes?
Nikolav: Yeah.
Noelle: *Looking at Dimitiri* And you, Dima, you just want Nico to be safe. You don't want him risking too much for change and getting hurt, right?
Dimitri: Exactly.
Noelle: Then I've got an idea. How about we go to the upcoming town hall this week? Nico, you could write a speech to give at the podium and be heard, and Dima, it will be much safer, And this would be good for me too, as you know Nico, I care about you <i> very </i> much too, so I'd also hate to see you get hurt, and I hate to see you to fight.
Both think about the option a little
Nikolav: Do you really think they will listen?
Dimitri: It is hard to say for sure, but that is the purpose of these meetings: to speak and be heard. If you think about it, we are doing this country a disservice by not speaking to them and using them as intended. Your mother and I can write speeches too to back you up, not to mention we are both cops, so people may listen to us a bit more.
Nikolav: And if they don't?
Dimitri: Then we try again next time. It's what your mother and I have been doing for so long with our higher-ups at work. Change comes slower, but it's safer.
* [Nikolav: *angrily* Why do I have to stay safe, what about other people?] ->whyme
* [Nikolav: Fine, I'll go] -> goodend
* [Nikolav: *Insultingly* Is your work the right way to make change? How much change have you made?...] -> angrypapa

== botheryou

Nikolav: {nicer: So it bothers you then? | Well? I asked a question. Does it bother you then?}
Dimitri: Yes and No. Yes, because just like you and your mother, I care about other people and don't want to see them suffer.
Dimitri: But no, in the sense that the protesters bring this on themselves by going about change in a more foolish, self-centered way. There are safer options people could try for change, like running for a government position or speaking to their representatives.
Noelle: That's an excellent point, dear! We all should go to the upcoming town hall and speak there! Nico can give a speech on change, and it will be much safer.
Nikolav: They are not going to listen
Dimitri: Your mother and I are cops; we have a little more sway, we can make them listen.
* [Nikolav: Fine, I'll go] -> goodend
* [Nikolav: We can't afford to do things the right way!] -> cantafford

== goodend

Nikolav: Fine, I'll go.
Noelle: Great! So how about we put off talking about this subject for another time, maybe when we are righting our pieces, and how about we just finish off this dinner by watching something nice like OldSheldon™ on the TV.
Nikolav: Fine.
Dimitri: That's a great idea, dear.
Noelle goes over and switches on the TV. The family migrates from the dining table to the TV room, and enjoys a good meal, albeit a little cold, and a good show. The argument has been postponed to a later date, and the scene fades out as the room is filled with studio laughter and bazingas™.

MINI SCENE END

-> END


== protest

Nikolav interrupts with a voice louder and more charged than expected.


Nikolav: If I can make wrong decisions, then I’m going to go to a protest!
Noelle: Sweetheart-
Dimitri: Let me clarify. You are allowed to make wrong decisions. But only when they don't matter. I don't care how you feel about protests; that's just an opinion.
Dimitri: But in decisions where there could be consequences, such as <b>going</b> to these events. I <b> will not</b> allow you to make the wrong decision. Such as with these riots.
Nikolav: <b>Protests.</b>
Noelle, sensing the rising tension, jumps in to mediate.
Noelle: Now, this is a tense topic, let's take care to hear eachother out and not talk over eachother. I didn't really wish to talk over this nice dinner Nico made and ruin it. - 
* [Nikolav: He already ruined it. He came two and a half hours late!]
~ ruined = true 
->late
* [Nikolav Doesn't interrupt] ->mamatime
* [Nikolav: *angrily* Why do I have to stay safe? What about everyone else?...] -> whyme

== antitv

Nikolav: It's fine, Mom, we don't need the TV. I can talk about something if you dislike silence.
Noelle: *Fiddling with the remote* I think I can find something better than this! Just give me a second - I find something not so divisive.
She starts to flip through the channels.
Dimitri: Divisive or not, it's important to acknowledge how protestors are treated in today’s world *he stops for a minute to take a bite of his food, emphasizing his point* <i> Not Well </i>
* [Nikolav: Doesn’t that bother you?] 
~ nicer = true 
-> botheryou
* [Nikolav: Maybe we need to change…] -> needforchange

== silence

Both Nikolav and Dimitri sit in silence, neither wishing to talk about current events.
After a little bit of fiddling, Noelle can change the channel on the critically acclaimed sitcom, OldSheldon™, which makes the perfect background noise.
She goes to sit down, but still wishes to talk a little.
Noelle: Nico, dear, how was your day?
He sits for a second, caught off guard by the question, then he provides the most teenager response.
Nikolav: Fine...
Noelle accepts this answer, but is understandably disappointed.
Dimitri: Surely you can give your mother a better answer than that
Nikolav: *With a little more anger* I'm <i>Fine</i> but...
* [Nikolav: You(Dimitri) were late to dinner.] -> late
* [Nikolav: The News bothers me.] -> botherme

== late

Nikolav:{ruined: He already ruined it. He came two and a half hours late! | You were late to dinner, now it's gotten cold and worse.}
Dimitri: Well, I'm sorry, dear, but I've been busy working to support this household, and I know you want change, so I've been working towards some changes at my job too.
* [Nikolav: *Insultingly* Is your work the right way to make change? How much change have you made?...] -> angrypapa
* [Nikolav: *muttering* I never asked you to work so much] -> whoasked

== whoasked

Nikolav mutters under his breath.
Nikolav: I never asked you to work so much...
This strikes a nerve with Dimitri.
Dimitri: No, you didn't. Maybe I should have asked you when you were a baby.
Dimitri: Nico, do you want me to go to work so you can have diapers?
Dimitri: Or maybe as a child.
Dimitri: Nico, do you want me to go to work so you can go to school?
Dimitri: Or maybe even I should ask now!
Dimitri: Nico, do you want me to go to work so you can have a home? A life? Anything else?
Nikolav: That's not what I meant! I mean, no one asked you to stay so late, or to work as a cop for all that it matters. You could just work a 9-5 somewhere!
Dimitri: Oh, Silly me, I forgot. Why am I busting my ass as a Cop when MuckNonalds is hiring!
Noelle: He doesn't mean it like that, dear-
Nikolav: No, I DO mean it like that. Why, out of all the jobs there are, why NOW, do you and Mom both have to be cops!
Dimitri slams his fist into the table.
Dimitri: BECAUSE OF THE WORLD.
He sits in silence for a few seconds.
Dimitri: Because of the world. We both agree it's not a good place. I just think being a police officer is a safer way to change it.
He stands up from the table, and neither of them may speak up after his uncharacteristic burst of anger.
Dimitri: *Looking at Noelle* I'll be in our room if you need me, dear.
With that, he stands up from the table and leaves.

MINI SCENE END

-> END

== botherme

Nikolav shifts in his chair uncomfortably, eventually deciding to address the Proboscidean in the room.
Nikolav: The News bothers me.
Noelle: Sorry, dear, I didn't mean to turn it on.
Dimitri: It's fine, honey, but I do agree it's unpleasant
* [Nikolav: So it bothers you?] 
~ nicer = true 
-> botheryou
* [Nikolav: Maybe we need to change.] -> needforchange

== needforchange

Nikolav: Maybe we need to change

Dimitri: I agree with you on that. We just need a more peaceful change. Protestors are going about things in the wrong way.


* [Nikolav: *Insultingly* Is your work the right way?...] -> angrypapa
* [Nikolav: We can't afford to do things the right way!...] -> cantafford

== angrypapa

Nikolav: *Insultingly* Is your work the right way? TELL ME, How much change have you made by being a good little police officer, licking the boots of the bureaucrats in power, defending their unjust rules and-
Dimitri: THAT IS ENOUGH!
Both Nikolav and Noelle are stunned by this sudden outburst
Dimitri: I work my ASS off daily to help make your life livable! You may hate my job now, but everything in this house, everything in your life, was paid for by my work for it!
Dimitri: You may hate it now, as you are a hormonal, short-sighted teen-
Nikolav: *Interupting* I'm not short-sighted, I just see the world as it is!
Dimitri: *Raising Voice* If you saw the world as it is, you'd realize just how dangerous these riots are! And you may hate my job, I won't ask for you to like it, I just ask you to respect it.
A long silence fills the room.
Nikolav: I'm sorry, but I don't think I can.
Dimitri: *Visibly disappointed* Then... I see no point in me being here. I'll be in my room.
He stands up from the table and starts to leave the room
Noelle: Honey, theres no need to leave, you should finishing your plate!
Dimitri: I'l' be fine, dear, I'm not that hungry anyway
And with that, he leaves. And the two remaining members sit in silence.

MINI SCENE END
-> END


== cantafford

Nikolav: We cannot afford to do things the right way! You've seen the way the government is acting. You've seen how it hurts people! I know you've seen it; you see it on the front lines every day at work!
Dimitri: *Heartbrokenly* Yes, I know, the government isn't well right now, but violent rebellion will just lead to more harm. Change is safer from the inside, like what your mother and I are working towards.
Noelle: Yes, dear, I agree with your father here. I've seen rebellions like this before. It may feel like you're fighting for freedom, but even if you get it and overthrow the government like you'd wish, people will fight over power once again. It's best not to push that far.
Nikolav: It's not about power, it's about being heard! Have you ever been able to change the minds of the higher-ups at your work?
Noelle and Dimitri both look at each other, frowning
Dimitri: We are not there yet, but we will be soon.
Noelle: Yes, and I get where you're coming from, dear, it's just- riots are too violent! I hope you understand why we don't want you, our sweet little Nico, getting hurt.
Nikolav: *Slamming his chair back and standing up* You don't care how many people get hurt, as long as it's not me, huh? Have you all no empathy?
Noelle: That's not what we-
Nikolav: *Storming away from the table* No, I've heard enough. I can't listen to any more of this. I'll be back tonight.
Before anyone can stop him. Nikolav storms out, slamming the door behind him.

MINI SCENE END
-> END

== whyme

Nikolav: Why does it only matter when I'm safe? What about the others! You don't care how many people get hurt, as long as it's not me, huh? Have you all no empathy?
Dimitri: Nico! Don't you dare say that, do you know how much your mother and risk every day for the people of this country?
Nikolav: Yes, you risk <i> So Much </i> by shutting down their protests
Noelle: Nico, you know your father and I don't work in the sector. And the reason why it matters that you are safe is because you are our son, you are our world.
Nikolav: It doesn't matter which sector you work in; you are still supporting an oppressive regime. And I may be your son, but those protestors on TV? They have parents, too, you know! They are sons and daughters, too! And the people being abused by the law and the government, they are people too!
Nikolav: But no one cares! No one listens! No one stands up for them! And if no one does, they will just be completely ignored and crushed!
Dimitri: Nico, we are trying our best-
Nikolav: *Storming away from the table* Well, it's enough! I'm going to go do it better. I'll be back tonight.
Noelle: NICO!
Dimitri: NIKOLAV DANGER SILVIA!
Before anyone can stop him. Nikolav storms out, slamming the door behind him.

MINI SCENE END
-> END
